{
  "name": "core-aliased",
  "description": "Aliased's names on a table, D147: a create gives the name, which no other row holds as a name or an alias in its normalized form (lower or slug), a name taken refused with the key of the row that holds it; rename keeps the old name as an alias; addAlias and removeAlias, a removed alias freed for another row; resolve on the table; a delete that frees the row's names; and the define refusals. Cases written by hand in the recorded format, since no engine implements Aliased. Each answer holds what the replayer compares: a record's id, data and behaviors, an operation's result, and a refusal whole, in the core's words; what only the engine's store answers (sequence numbers, versions, timestamps, the document a define echoes) is left out.",
  "source": "written by hand (D147): runtime/engine/testdata/rules/scenarios/core-aliased.json",
